      "body": "Is there a use case to expose the pow-consensus rules? the deployment-consensus rules are not exposed either, neither is the full raw genesis block hex. Also, any code calling this and wanting to do pow checks on (let's say bip94 rules) will have write code to implement bip94. So that code can just be triggered by `if chain_type_string == \"testnet4\": ...`\r\n\r\nSo I think, any code calling this will either not care about those  consensus rules, or will have to implement the exact pow-rules for that chain type string themselves anyway. In both cases there is no use case for this?",
      "created_at": "2026-07-17T07:28:57Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-07-17T07:41:01Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35736#discussion_r3601219007",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
